# Mesa patch series for GFX1013 (BC-250), applied in order against
# pristine mesa-26.2.4 with `git apply` / `patch -p1`.
#
# Patches 0001-0007 from MastaG/linux-cachyos-bc250 (Oct 2026 sync,
# patches/mesa/ stable series for Mesa 26.2.4).
#
# 0001: Expose ACE compute queue + async compute threadgroup workaround.
#       Always active.
# 0002: DirectMesh v1.3 (lonewolf0622/bc250meshtaskwork) — VK_EXT_mesh_shader
#       Mesh AND Task + VK_KHR_fragment_shader_barycentric + no-op VRS +
#       VK_EXT_device_generated_commands + multiview + indexed Mesh draws.
#       Replaces the old GFX10.3-spoof path (0002-0004 in the previous
#       series); RADV_GFX103 is gone. Off unless RADV_DIRECTMESH=1 is set
#       per game — never affects other GPUs or default rendering.
# 0003: FSR4 V3 deferred SDot — MAD24 chains, dense SDot pre-pass,
#       deferred lowering round. Always active.
# 0004: FSR4 combined-unroll selection — NIR pattern matching. Active by
#       default.
# 0005: FSR4 image-preparation and texture candidates (opt-in envs,
#       flipped on by 0007).
# 0006: FSR4 resolution-variant coverage and 8K store guard.
# 0007: FSR4 production defaults — enables all FSR4 optimizations.
#
# Alternative: patches/mesa-native-mesh/series uses lonewolf0622's native
# mesh approach (MESH only, no TASK) — mostly superseded by DirectMesh;
# kept for users who need the smallest possible delta.

0001-gfx1013-compute-queue-fix.patch
0002-bc250-directmesh.patch
0003-bc250-fsr4-v3.patch
0004-bc250-fsr4-combined-unroll.patch
0005-bc250-fsr4-imageprep-texture.patch
0006-bc250-fsr4-resolution-variants.patch
0007-bc250-fsr4-production-defaults.patch
